    <mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" padding="1px 1px 1px 1px" border-radius="10px">
  <mj-column background-color="#fff" border-radius="10px" padding="0px">
    <mj-image
      border-radius="10px 10px 0 0"
      padding="0"
      width="600px"
      src="https://www.londonsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
      alt="School antisemitism review"
      href="https://www.londonsummary.com/"
    />
    <mj-text
      padding="20px 20px 0px 20px"
      font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
      color="#000000"
    >
      <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
        School antisemitism review
      </h2>
    </mj-text>
    <mj-text padding="0px 20px 0px 20px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>What’s happening?</strong> Britain’s government has launched an independent review into <a href="https://uk.news.yahoo.com/britain-launches-review-school-related-104628475.html" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">antisemitism in England’s schools and colleges</a>. The review will evaluate how schools identify, prevent, and respond to antisemitic behaviour, examine incident-handling policies, and assess how external factors, such as protests and geopolitical tensions, affect student conduct within educational environments. The review will also evaluate the training and guidance provided to teachers and staff.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>Why?</strong> The Community Security Trust recorded 204 antisemitic incidents linked to education settings in 2025. Nationally, reported antisemitism rose 4% that year, the second-highest total on record. Jewish students and teachers have raised concerns about hostility, harassment, and a lack of effective responses when incidents occur.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; padding-top: 15px; padding-bottom: 20px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>Big picture:</strong> Since the Gaza war began after Hamas’s October 7 attacks, antisemitic incidents have risen in several Western countries, raising fears about the safety of Jewish communities and the resilience of social cohesion. In Britain, classrooms have become a focal point where political debates, protests, and online narratives spill into student behaviour. Government review aims to curb antisemitism while balancing debate and school safety.
</p>
    </mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-spacer height="20px" />
