<mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" padding="1px 1px 1px 1px" border-radius="10px">
  <mj-column background-color="#fff" border-radius="10px" padding="0px">
    <mj-image
      border-radius="10px 10px 0 0"
      padding="0"
      width="600px"
      src="https://www.londonsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
      alt="Faiths fast together"
      href="https://www.londonsummary.com/"
    />
    <mj-text
      padding="20px 20px 0px 20px"
      font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
      color="#000000"
    >
      <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
        Faiths fast together
      </h2>
    </mj-text>
    <mj-text padding="0px 20px 0px 20px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>What’s happening? </strong>For the <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cn8z2ng73pxo" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">first time since 1993</a>, the Islamic holy month of Ramadan and the Christian season of Lent have begun at roughly the same time. In London, communities of different faiths are observing their respective practices while recognising similarities. Muslims fast daily from sunrise to sunset during Ramadan, breaking the fast with iftar meals, while Christians observing Lent focus on prayer, fasting, and acts of self-discipline over 40 days leading to Easter.  <br><br><strong>Similarities:</strong> Ramadan and Lent share several spiritual and social similarities. Both are periods of fasting, prayer, reflection, and self-discipline. Observers are encouraged to practice humility, charity, and compassion toward others. Both traditions emphasise spiritual growth over physical sacrifice, reminding believers to focus on gratitude, forgiveness, and moral responsibility. Community also plays a key role, with people gathering for prayers, meals, and acts of service.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; padding-top: 15px; padding-bottom: 20px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>Big picture:</strong> The overlap of Ramadan and Lent highlights how different religions often share similar spiritual practices and values. In diverse cities like London, this coincidence has become an opportunity for interfaith dialogue and cultural understanding. At a time of global tensions and religious divisions, the simultaneous observance of these traditions serves as a reminder that many faiths share similar goals of compassion, humility, and spiritual renewal.
</p>
    </mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-spacer height="20px" />
    
