  ">
    <a href="https://www.birminghammail.co.uk/news/uk-news/british-railway-company-collapses-liquidation-33527603" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">IRD Railway Services Limited, a long-standing supplier of specialist track-related products and services to the UK railway industry, entered voluntary liquidation</a>. The decision was approved at a shareholder meeting where members passed resolutions to wind up the company. Insolvency specialists Gareth Howarth and Philip Lawrence from AMS Business Recovery were appointed as joint liquidators to oversee the process.
