    <a href="https://news.sky.com/story/millions-of-drivers-set-to-get-motor-finance-compensation-this-year-watchdog-announces-13514972" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">Britain’s financial regulator, the Financial Conduct Authority, is preparing a compensation scheme for drivers affected by the UK’s mis-sold motor finance scandal</a>. If approved, lenders will have three to five months to compensate customers. A review in 2021 found many brokers and dealers used discretionary commission arrangements, increasing loan interest rates without clearly informing customers to earn higher commissions.
  </td>
</tr>
